{"availability":"available","full":"sarsamurmu/estree-toolkit","name":"estree-toolkit","description":"Tools for working with ESTree AST","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":71,"forks":4,"created":"2020-12-28T13:18:17Z","updated":"2026-05-05T06:27:44Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://estree-toolkit.netlify.app/","topics":["acorn","analysis","ast","fast","javascript","meriyah","scope","traversal","typescript","visitor","walker"],"demo":"https://estree-toolkit.netlify.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T21:08:22.106Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T21:08:22.106Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T21:08:22.106Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T21:08:22.106Z","stars":71,"forks":4}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["There are several static utilities that you can use.","Evaluates the path for truthiness and returns true, false or undefined depending on evaluation result.","I know there is Babel. But there are other tools which are faster than Babel. For example, meriyah is 3x faster than @babel/parser, astring is up to 50x faster than @babel/generator. But these tool only work with ESTree AST. I wanted to use these faster alternatives for one of my projects but could not find any traverser with batteries-included. So I built one myself, with awesome scope analysis, it has all the things that you would need for traversing an ESTree AST. Also, a little bit faster than Babel."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sarsamurmu/estree-toolkit/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"c77a2de6c4997c9633ff12c923c6fbba84e5168f9f1db23c08e7e922740cf586","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T21:08:22.285Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T21:08:22.285Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"There are several static utilities that you can use.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sarsamurmu/estree-toolkit/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"c77a2